#: ../../source/assy.rst:281
msgid "``hold*Force`` ``hold*ForceMin`` ``hold*ForceMax``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/assy.rst:286
msgid ""
"Pushing an object into place is a linear motion, so ``pushForceMax`` "
"bounds a **force** in newtons. Turning it is a rotation, so "
"``turnTorqueMax`` bounds a **torque** in newton-metres."
msgstr ""
"把对象推入到位是一种直线运动，因此 ``pushForceMax`` 限定的是以牛顿为单位的 **力** 。转动它则是一种旋转，因此 `"
"`turnTorqueMax`` 限定的是以牛顿·米为单位的 **力矩** 。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:292
msgid ""
"``pushForceMax`` was called ``pushTorqueMax`` in the first draft of this "
"section. The old spelling is still accepted, with a warning, and means "
"the same thing."
msgstr ""
"在本节的初稿中， ``pushForceMax`` 曾被称作 ``pushTorqueMax`` 。旧写法目前仍被接受（并伴随一条警告）"
"，含义完全相同。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:296
msgid ""
"`threadStep` is the **lead**: the axial distance the object advances per "
"full turn. For a multi-start thread that is the pitch multiplied by the "
"number of starts, not the pitch itself. When it is non-zero, the "
"assembler manages the pushing force and the turning torque together, so "
"that the resulting motion reproduces the given thread (or, more "
"generally, rotation) pattern, staying within `pushForceMax` and "
"`turnTorqueMax`. The default of `0.00` means a straight push with no "
"turning."
msgstr ""
"`threadStep` 是 **导程** ：对象每转一整圈所前进的轴向距离。对于多头螺纹，它等于螺距乘以头数，而不是螺距本身。当它非零"
"时，装配器会把推力和转动力矩放在一起管理，使最终的运动复现所给定的螺纹（更一般地说，是旋转）规律，并始终保持在 `pushForceMa"
"x` 和 `turnTorqueMax` 的范围之内。默认值 `0.00` 表示只做直线推入、不做转动。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:304
msgid ""
"A thread belongs to the interfaces rather than to any one connection, so "
"it is normally declared there and left out here - see :ref:`interface-"
"thread` below. Given on a connection, it overrides what the interfaces "
"say for that one step."
msgstr ""
"螺纹属于接口，而不属于某一个单独的连接，因此它通常在接口那里声明、在这里省略——参见下文的 :ref:`interface-thread"
"` 。若在某个连接上给出了它，它会在那一个步骤中覆盖接口的说法。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:308
msgid ""
"`pushDirection` is not a field: it is deduced from the connection itself "
"and reported alongside the rest. It is the direction, in the assembly's "
"coordinates, that the object travels while it is pushed into place - so "
"the object starts at `pushDistance` back along it."
msgstr ""
"`pushDirection` 不是一个字段：它由连接本身推导得出，并与其余内容一同报告。它是在装配体坐标系中，对象被推入到位时所行进的"
"方向——因此对象的起点就在沿该方向回退 `pushDistance` 处。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:313
msgid ""
"The interfaces are what it is deduced from. The positive Z axis of an "
"interface points **into** the object the interface belongs to, which is "
"exactly the way a part coming to meet it has to travel. "
"`examples/feature_interface` shows this directly: both faces of the same "
"3mm bracket are instances of one interface, the ``outer`` one at ``z=0`` "
"unrotated and the ``inner`` one at ``z=3`` turned around, so the two axes"
" point at each other through the material. Each of the four M3 screws in "
"that example is connected to one of those faces, and its deduced "
"direction points from the screw through the bracket towards the motor - "
"reversing, as it must, when the motor is placed on the other side."
msgstr ""
"推导的依据正是接口。接口的 Z 轴正方向指向该接口所属对象的 **内部** ，而这恰恰就是前来与之相接的零件必须行进的方向。 `exam"
"ples/feature_interface`  直接展示了这一点：同一块 3mm 支架的两个面都是同一个接口的实例， ``outer`"
"` 那个位于 ``z=0`` 且未旋转， ``inner`` 那个位于 ``z=3`` 且被翻转过来，于是两条轴穿过材料彼此相对。该示例"
"中的四颗 M3 螺钉各自连接到其中一个面上，其推导出的方向从螺钉穿过支架指向电机——而当电机被放到另一侧时，这个方向也必然随之反向。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:323
msgid ""
"`pushDistance` is how far away from its final place the object starts: "
"the distance, along `pushDirection`, between the staging pose and the "
"pose where its `with` ports coincide with the target's `to` ports. When "
"it is omitted, it is derived from the object being connected, as **1.5 "
"times that object's own length along the Z axis of the interface "
"location** it is connected by - far enough for the object to clear the "
"target before the insertion move begins. That measurement needs the "
"object's geometry, so it is made only when something asks for it, never "
"while the assembly is merely being instantiated. If the geometry cannot "
"be built at all, the distance is reported as unset rather than guessed."
msgstr ""
"`pushDistance` 是对象的起点距其最终位置有多远：即沿 `pushDirection` 方向，预备位姿与其 `with` 端"
"口和目标的 `to` 端口重合时的位姿之间的距离。省略它时，该值由被连接的对象推导得出，取为 **该对象自身沿其所用接口位置的 Z 轴方"
"向的长度的 1.5 倍** ——这足以让对象在插入动作开始之前与目标完全错开。这项测量需要对象的几何体，因此只有在有需求时才会进行，绝不"
"会仅因为装配体被实例化就去做。如果几何体根本无法构建，该距离会报告为未设置，而不是去猜测。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:334
msgid ""
"`stage` names a group of steps that are expected to be connected **at the"
" same time** rather than one after another: consecutive nodes carrying "
"the same `stage` form one such group. It is a free-form label, so it can "
"say what the group is for. A `stage` that is interrupted by another one "
"and then resumes is reported, since the steps it names are then not "
"consecutive and will not be performed together."
msgstr ""
"`stage` 命名的是一组预期 **同时** 连接、而不是一个接一个连接的步骤：带有相同 `stage` 的连续节点构成这样的一组。它"
"是自由格式的标签，因此可以说明这一组是做什么用的。如果某个 `stage` 被另一个打断之后又恢复，系统会报告这一情况，因为它所指的那些"
"步骤此时并不连续，也就不会被同时执行。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:362
msgid ""
"`holdWith` names the interface of the object that is getting added to the"
" assembly, to be used to hold that object while it is connected. `holdTo`"
" names the interface of the object that is already in the assembly, which"
" is held the same way. Either may be a single interface name or a list of"
" them."
msgstr ""
"`holdWith` 指名正在被添加到装配体中的那个对象的接口，用于在连接过程中握持该对象。 `holdTo` 指名已经存在于装配体中的"
"那个对象的接口，它以同样的方式被握持。两者都可以是单个接口名称，也可以是一组接口名称的列表。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:383
msgid ""
"When `holdWith` is omitted, it defaults to the `hold` field of the "
"`connect` section of the part or the assembly being added (see "
":ref:`hold`). When `holdTo` is omitted, it defaults to the `hold` field "
"of the object being connected to. When neither is set, the assembler is "
"free to hold the object however it sees fit."
msgstr ""
"省略 `holdWith` 时，它默认取被添加的零件或装配体的 `connect` 一节中的 `hold` 字段（参见 :ref:`ho"
"ld` ）。省略 `holdTo` 时，它默认取被连接到的那个对象的 `hold` 字段。两者都未设置时，装配器可以按它认为合适的任何方"
"式握持该对象。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:388
msgid ""
"`holdWithInstance` and `holdToInstance` select which instance of the "
"interface to hold by, for the cases where the object implements more than"
" one instance of it. They are matched positionally against `holdWith` and"
" `holdTo`. When omitted, the instance defaults to the `holdInstance` "
"field of that same section, and, failing that, to the first instance of "
"the interface."
msgstr ""
"`holdWithInstance` 和 `holdToInstance` 用于选择按接口的哪一个实例来握持，适用于对象实现了该接口的多"
"个实例的情形。它们按位置与 `holdWith` 和 `holdTo` 相对应。省略时，实例默认取同一节中的 `holdInstance"
"` 字段；若仍没有，则取该接口的第一个实例。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:394
msgid ""
"`holdWithForceMin` and `holdWithForceMax` bound the force each end is "
"held with, in newtons - enough to keep the object from moving, not so "
"much as to damage it. `holdWithForce` sets both at once, and "
"`holdToForce*` are the same for the object being connected to. Each bound"
" is resolved on its own, from the first of these that gives it:"
msgstr ""
"`holdWithForceMin` 和 `holdWithForceMax` 限定握持每一端所用的力，单位为牛顿——足以让对象不发生移"
"动，又不至于损坏它。 `holdWithForce` 一次性设置两者，而 `holdToForce*` 对被连接到的那个对象起同样的作用"
"。每个边界值各自独立解析，取下列来源中第一个给出它的："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:400
msgid "the bound itself, `holdWithForceMin` or `holdWithForceMax`;"
msgstr "边界值本身，即 `holdWithForceMin` 或 `holdWithForceMax` ；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:401
msgid "`holdWithForce`, which sets both;"
msgstr "`holdWithForce` ，它同时设置两者；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:402
msgid ""
"the `holdForceMin`/`holdForceMax` field of the `connect` section of the "
"part or the assembly (see :ref:`hold`);"
msgstr ""
"零件或装配体的 `connect` 一节中的 `holdForceMin` / `holdForceMax` 字段（参见 :ref:`h"
"old` ）；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:404
msgid "the `holdForce` field of that same section, which sets both;"
msgstr "同一节中的 `holdForce` 字段，它同时设置两者；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:405
msgid "the defaults, **3 N** for the minimum and **7 N** for the maximum."
msgstr "默认值，最小值为 **3 N** ，最大值为 **7 N** 。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:407
msgid ""
"A minimum that ends up above its maximum is a contradiction rather than a"
" range: it is reported, and both bounds fall back to the defaults."
msgstr "最终高于其最大值的最小值是一个矛盾，而不是一个区间：这会被报告，并且两个边界值都回退到默认值。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:413
msgid "The thread of an interface"
msgstr "接口的螺纹"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:415
msgid ""
"An interface may declare the thread that connections made through it "
"advance along, and whether it cuts its own:"
msgstr "接口可以声明：通过它建立的连接沿着怎样的螺纹前进，以及它是否自行切出螺纹："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:426
msgid ""
"Both are inherited by the interfaces that inherit this one, so a thread "
"is spelled out once, on the interface that introduces it. In "
"`examples/feature_interface` the abstract `m3` interface carries `0.5` "
"and the abstract `m4` carries `0.7` - the real pitches of those screws - "
"and every opening, screw and hole pattern derived from them connects with"
" the right thread without repeating it."
msgstr ""
"这两项都会被继承该接口的那些接口所继承，因此螺纹只需在引入它的那个接口上写明一次。在 `examples/feature_interfa"
"ce` 中，抽象接口 `m3` 带有 `0.5` ，抽象接口 `m4` 带有 `0.7` ——即这些螺钉的真实螺距——而由它们派生出的每"
"一个开口、螺钉和孔位阵列，都无需重复声明就能以正确的螺纹进行连接。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:433
msgid ""
"A connection inherits `threadStep` from the two interfaces it mates. They"
" have to agree on it: two different threads cannot be screwed together, "
"and a connection whose ends disagree is reported and fails ``pc test``. "
"Unless, that is, one of them declares `selfScrew` - a self-tapping screw,"
" or the plain hole one goes into. Then the thread of the end that does "
"have to match one is the thread that gets cut, and failing that the one "
"the self-tapping end brings with it."
msgstr ""
"连接会从它所配合的两个接口继承 `threadStep` 。两者必须在这一点上一致：两种不同的螺纹无法拧在一起，两端不一致的连接会被报告"
"，并使 ``pc test`` 失败。除非其中一端声明了 `selfScrew` ——比如自攻螺钉，或者它所拧入的普通光孔。这时，确实必"
"须与之匹配的那一端的螺纹，就是被切出来的那个螺纹；若没有这样的一端，则采用自攻的那一端自身带来的螺纹。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:442
msgid "How a mating goes together"
msgstr "配合是如何装到一起的"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:444
msgid ""
"A pair of interfaces that always goes together the same way - an M3 screw"
" into an M3 tapped hole, a clip onto its rail - says so once, in a "
"``how`` section of its mating, instead of on every connection:"
msgstr ""
"总是以同一种方式装到一起的一对接口——M3 螺钉拧入 M3 攻丝孔、卡扣扣上它的导轨——只需在其配合的 ``how`` 一节中声明一次，"
"而不必在每个连接上都写一遍："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:465
msgid ""
"It takes the fields of a connection's ``how`` that say how the object "
"goes in: ``pushForceMax``, ``pushDistance``, ``turnDirection``, "
"``turnTorqueMax``, ``threadStep``, ``selfScrew`` and ``snapIn``. "
"``stage`` is not one of them - which steps are done together is the "
"assembly's to say - and nor are the ``hold*`` fields, which belong to the"
" objects (see :ref:`hold`)."
msgstr ""
"它接受连接的 ``how`` 中那些说明对象如何进入的字段： ``pushForceMax`` 、 ``pushDistance`` 、"
" ``turnDirection`` 、 ``turnTorqueMax`` 、 ``threadStep`` 、 ``selfScre"
"w`` 和 ``snapIn`` 。 ``stage`` 不在其中——哪些步骤一起完成由装配体来决定—— ``hold*`` 这些字段也"
"不在其中，它们属于对象（参见 :ref:`hold` ）。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:471
msgid ""
"Every connection made through the pair gets them, and an ASSY file "
"overrides them **field by field**: a step whose own ``how`` gives only "
"``turnTorqueMax`` keeps the mating's thread and direction. The order, "
"most specific first, is the connection's ``how``, the mating's ``how``, "
"the mating's own ``selfScrew`` and ``snapIn``, the interfaces' "
"``threadStep`` and ``selfScrew``, and the defaults."
msgstr ""
"通过这一对接口建立的每个连接都会获得这些设置，而 ASSY 文件会 **逐个字段地** 覆盖它们：一个自身的 ``how`` 只给出了 "
"``turnTorqueMax`` 的步骤，仍保留配合所给的螺纹和方向。按从最具体到最一般的顺序依次是：连接的 ``how`` 、配合的"
" ``how`` 、配合自身的 ``selfScrew`` 和 ``snapIn`` 、接口的 ``threadStep`` 和 ``s"
"elfScrew`` ，最后是默认值。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:478
msgid "Reading the instructions back"
msgstr "回读装配说明"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:480
msgid ""
"Everything resolved from the sections above - the inherited threads, the "
"deduced push direction, the forces each end is held with - is reported by"
msgstr "由上述各节解析得出的一切——继承而来的螺纹、推导出的推入方向、握持每一端所用的力——都会由以下命令报告"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:487
msgid ""
"under ``Connections``, one entry per connected object. That is the "
"assembly's own account of how it is built, for a person or for whatever "
"performs it."
msgstr ""
"报告位于 ``Connections`` 之下，每个被连接的对象对应一条记录。这就是装配体对自己如何被装配出来的说明，既供人阅读，也供执"
"行装配的任何一方使用。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:491
msgid "Testing the instructions"
msgstr "测试装配说明"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:493
msgid ""
"Everything above is resolved leniently: a field that is missing takes its"
" default, and one that contradicts itself is reported and replaced with a"
" default, so that an assembly always builds. ``pc test`` is what looks "
"past that leniency. Its ``connect`` test fails an assembly whose "
"instructions had to be repaired to be usable, and passes one that is "
"sound - **including one that says nothing at all** and takes every "
"default."
msgstr ""
"上面的一切都是宽松解析的：缺失的字段取其默认值，自相矛盾的字段会被报告并替换为默认值，这样装配体总能构建出来。 ``pc test`` "
"正是越过这种宽松去审视的那一环。它的 ``connect`` 测试会让那些必须经过修复才可用的装配说明不通过，而让本身就健全的装配说明通"
"过—— **包括什么都没说、全部采用默认值的那种** 。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:500
msgid "What it rejects today:"
msgstr "它目前会拒绝的情况："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:502
msgid ""
"a ``*Min`` above its corresponding ``*Max`` - ``holdWithForceMin`` above "
"``holdWithForceMax``, or ``holdToForceMin`` above ``holdToForceMax``. A "
"minimum above a maximum is a contradiction rather than a range."
msgstr ""
"某个 ``*Min`` 高于与之对应的 ``*Max`` —— ``holdWithForceMin`` 高于 ``holdWithFo"
"rceMax`` ，或者 ``holdToForceMin`` 高于 ``holdToForceMax`` 。高于最大值的最小值是一个矛"
"盾，而不是一个区间。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:505
msgid ""
"two interfaces that disagree about their `threadStep` with neither "
"declaring `selfScrew`."
msgstr "两个接口的 `threadStep` 不一致，而且两者都没有声明 `selfScrew` 。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:513
msgid "Steps that can be followed"
msgstr "可以照着做的步骤"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:515
msgid ""
"Defaults are enough for an assembly to build, and they are not enough for"
" a person to put it together. So an assembly that is meant to be made "
"(``manufacturable: true``) is held to more by ``pc test``: every item "
"after the first of each list of links has to be connected (``connect`` or"
" ``connectPorts``), and something has to say **how** it goes into place -"
" pushed, snapped or screwed in. That is said by any of:"
msgstr ""
"默认值足以让装配体构建出来，却不足以让人把它装配起来。因此，对于打算真正制造出来的装配体（ ``manufacturable: true"
"`` ）， ``pc test`` 的要求更高：每个链接列表中第一项之后的每一项都必须是连接起来的（ ``connect`` 或 ``c"
"onnectPorts`` ），并且必须有某处说明它 **以何种方式** 被安放到位——是推入、卡入还是拧入。下列任何一处都可以说明这一点："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:522
msgid ""
"the connection's own ``how``, with at least one of ``pushForceMax``, "
"``pushDistance``, ``turnDirection``, ``turnTorqueMax``, ``threadStep``, "
"``selfScrew`` or ``snapIn`` (``stage`` and the ``hold*`` fields say when "
"and by what, not how);"
msgstr ""
"连接自身的 ``how`` ，其中至少给出 ``pushForceMax`` 、 ``pushDistance`` 、 ``turnDi"
"rection`` 、 ``turnTorqueMax`` 、 ``threadStep`` 、 ``selfScrew`` 或 ``s"
"napIn`` 之一（ ``stage`` 和 ``hold*`` 这些字段说明的是何时以及用什么来做，而不是以何种方式）；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:526
msgid ""
"the mating of the two interfaces it connects through: any field of its "
"``how`` (see \"How a mating goes together\" above), or its own ``snapIn``"
" or ``selfScrew``, which then says it for every connection that pairs "
"them;"
msgstr ""
"它所通过的那两个接口之间的配合：该配合的 ``how`` 的任意字段（参见上文“配合是如何装到一起的”），或者配合自身的 ``snapI"
"n`` 或 ``selfScrew`` ——这样一来，凡是把这两个接口配成一对的连接都得到了说明；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:529
msgid ""
"the interfaces themselves, with a ``threadStep`` or ``selfScrew``: a "
"thread is screwed in."
msgstr "接口本身，带有 ``threadStep`` 或 ``selfScrew`` ：有螺纹就意味着拧入。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:532
msgid ""
"The ``manufacturability`` test reports each step that says none of these;"
" an item placed by ``location:`` is the ``connectivity`` test's to "
"report. The IDE's Build vs Buy table shows an assembly with such steps as"
" **Incomplete**, listing them, until they are fixed."
msgstr ""
"``manufacturability`` 测试会报告每一个这些都没有说明的步骤；而由 ``location:`` 放置的项，则交由 `"
"`connectivity`` 测试来报告。在这些步骤被修正之前，IDE 的 Build vs Buy 表格会把含有此类步骤的装配体显示"
"为 **Incomplete** ，并把它们逐一列出。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:540
msgid "Holding an object"
msgstr "握持对象"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:542
msgid ""
"The defaults for the `how` fields above are declared once, next to the "
"part or the assembly itself, in `partcad.yaml`:"
msgstr "上述 `how` 字段的默认值，只需在 `partcad.yaml` 中、紧挨着零件或装配体本身声明一次："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:563
msgid ""
"Everything an object contributes to every connection it takes part in "
"lives in that one `connect` section, rather than among the fields that "
"describe the object itself."
msgstr "一个对象为它所参与的每一个连接所贡献的全部内容，都放在那一个 `connect` 一节里，而不是混在描述该对象本身的那些字段之中。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:571
msgid "Scenes"
msgstr "场景"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:573
msgid ""
"The same file format defines a **scene**: a placed arrangement of "
"objects, such as a workcell, a table with parts laid out on it, or a "
"simulation world. A package declares one by pointing at the file from its"
" ``scenes:`` section rather than its ``assemblies:`` section (see "
":ref:`scenes`); there is no assembly object in between, and nothing about"
" the file itself says which it is."
msgstr ""
"同一种文件格式也用来定义 **场景** ：一组摆放好的对象，比如一个工作单元、一张摆放着零件的桌子，或者一个仿真世界。包通过从它的 ``"
"scenes:`` 一节、而不是 ``assemblies:`` 一节指向该文件来声明一个场景（参见 :ref:`scenes` ）；中"
"间不存在装配体对象，并且文件本身没有任何地方说明它究竟是哪一种。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:585
msgid ""
"Everything above applies, with one exception: **a scene may not use** "
"``how``. An assembly is a product and says how it is put together, which "
"is what the assembly instruction book is generated from. A scene states "
"only an end state, and nothing in it was assembled, so there is nothing "
"to say about the assembling. Declaring ``how`` in a scene is an error, "
"both while the scene is being built and in the editor."
msgstr ""
"上面的一切都同样适用，只有一个例外： **场景不得使用** ``how`` 。装配体是一件产品，它说明自己是如何装配起来的，装配说明书正"
"是据此生成的。而场景只陈述一个最终状态，其中没有任何东西是被装配出来的，因此也就无从谈起装配过程。在场景中声明 ``how`` 是一个错"
"误，构建场景时和在编辑器中都是如此。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:592
msgid ""
"The ``connect`` and ``connectPorts`` sections themselves stay. Placing a "
"gripper against the fixture it holds is a statement about where things "
"are, and saying it with the ports the two objects declare is better than "
"saying it with coordinates somebody worked out by hand."
msgstr ""
"``connect`` 和 ``connectPorts`` 这两节本身仍然保留。把夹爪放到它所夹持的夹具上，陈述的是各物体所处的位置，"
"而用这两个对象所声明的端口来表述它，要好过用某个人手工算出来的坐标。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:615
msgid "Part of an assembly"
msgstr "装配体的一部分"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:617
msgid ""
"A sub-assembly worth looking at on its own is often not an object of its "
"own: the head of the logo, one bay of a rack, the parts that arrive in "
"one box. A **filter** names the links to keep and leaves the rest out."
msgstr ""
"值得单独查看的子装配体，往往并不是一个独立的对象：标志的头部、机架的某一格、装在同一个箱子里送来的那些零件。 **过滤器** 指名要保留"
"哪些链接，并把其余的排除在外。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:621
msgid ""
"A filter is a tree of link names mirroring the tree the ASSY file already"
" is:"
msgstr "过滤器是一棵由链接名称构成的树，它与 ASSY 文件本身的那棵树相对应："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:629
msgid "Three rules, and nothing else:"
msgstr "只有三条规则，再无其他："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:631
msgid "a link the filter names is kept, and a link it does not name is dropped;"
msgstr "过滤器指名的链接予以保留，它未指名的链接则被丢弃；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:632
msgid "a link named with nothing under it keeps everything under it;"
msgstr "被指名、但其下没有写任何内容的链接，保留它下面的全部内容；"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:633
msgid ""
"a link named with at least one child under it keeps those children and "
"drops its other ones."
msgstr "被指名、且其下至少写了一个子节点的链接，保留这些子节点，并丢弃它的其他子节点。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:636
msgid ""
"A link is named the way :ref:`everything else names it <assy-link-"
"names>`: its ``name:``, the part or the assembly it places, or its "
"position in its ``links:`` list. So there is no link a filter cannot "
"name."
msgstr ""
"链接的指名方式与 :ref:`其他各处指名它的方式 <assy-link-names>` 相同：它的 ``name:`` 、它所放置的零"
"件或装配体，或者它在所属 ``links:`` 列表中的位置。因此，不存在过滤器无法指名的链接。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:640
msgid ""
"A filter may equally be written as a list, which is the convenient form "
"when nothing below the names matters:"
msgstr "过滤器同样可以写成一个列表；当名称之下的内容都无关紧要时，这是更方便的写法："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:648
msgid "There are three ways to use one, and they do different things."
msgstr "过滤器有三种用法，它们所做的事情各不相同。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:651
msgid "Filtering for one picture"
msgstr "为某一张图进行过滤"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:653
msgid ""
"``pc render`` and ``pc export`` take ``--filter``, and write nothing into"
" the package: the assembly is built as it always is and the filter is "
"applied to the result, for this one file."
msgstr ""
"``pc render`` 和 ``pc export`` 接受 ``--filter`` ，并且不会向包中写入任何内容：装配体照常构建"
"，过滤器只作用于构建结果，且仅针对这一个文件。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:663
msgid ""
"The argument is a **filename first**: a file somebody keeps beside the "
"package and edits. Only when there is no such file is the text read as "
"the filter itself, as JSON or YAML -- which is the convenient form for "
"one link and for whatever a script composes. A name that is neither is "
"refused, naming both things that went wrong, so a mistyped filename is "
"not quietly read as a link name."
msgstr ""
"该参数 **首先被当作文件名** ：一个有人保存在包旁边并加以编辑的文件。只有在不存在这样的文件时，这段文本才会被当作过滤器本身、按 J"
"SON 或 YAML 来读取——对于只有一个链接的情形，以及脚本临时拼出来的内容，这是更方便的写法。两者都不是的名称会被拒绝，并同时指出"
"两方面的问题，这样拼错的文件名就不会被悄悄当成链接名称。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:670
msgid ""
"Everything kept stays where the whole assembly put it. A filter never re-"
"resolves a ``connect:``, which is the only reading of \"part of this "
"assembly\" that is true of the thing on the bench. Because the result is "
"built rather than written, a filter here may also select *inside* a link "
"that places an assembly of another package."
msgstr ""
"保留下来的一切都停留在整个装配体为它安排的位置上。过滤器绝不会重新解析 ``connect:`` ——对于工作台上的实物而言，这是“这个"
"装配体的一部分”唯一成立的理解方式。由于这里的结果是构建出来的、而不是写出来的，因此这里的过滤器也可以在放置了另一个包的装配体的那个链接"
" *内部* 进行选择。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:676
msgid ""
"The same options are available in the `PartCAD extension for VS Code "
"<https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=PartCAD.partcad-"
"official>`_: the **2D** and **Draft** tabs of the viewer list what the "
"object is made of beside the drawing, with a checkbox on every item, and "
"what is ticked is the filter the render is made with. On the 2D tab the "
"list also holds each node's ports and interfaces, and ticking one draws "
"that port on the projection -- the same thing ``--with-ports``, ``--with-"
"interfaces`` and ``--port`` ask for. All three Design tabs share one "
"selection, so what is ticked on the 3D view is what the 2D and Draft tabs"
" draw, and a box cleared on one is cleared on the others."
msgstr ""
"`面向 VS Code 的 PartCAD 扩展 <https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items"
"?itemName=PartCAD.partcad-official>`_ 中也提供了同样的选项：查看器的 **2D** 和 **Dra"
"ft** 标签页会在图形旁边列出该对象由什么构成，每一项都带一个复选框，被勾选的内容就是本次渲染所使用的过滤器。在 2D 标签页上，该列"
"表还包含每个节点的端口和接口，勾选其中之一就会把那个端口画到投影上——这与 ``--with-ports`` 、 ``--with-in"
"terfaces`` 和 ``--port`` 所要求的是同一件事。三个 Design 标签页共享同一份选择，因此在 3D 视图上勾选的"
"内容，就是 2D 和 Draft 标签页所绘制的内容，在其中一个上取消勾选，另外两个上也随之取消。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:687
msgid "Filtering every time the file is written"
msgstr "每次写出文件时都进行过滤"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:689
msgid ""
"A ``filter:`` on a ``render:`` or ``export:`` file type says the same "
"thing permanently, so a package can keep a picture of one sub-assembly "
"checked in beside the drawing of the whole of it. It is declared per file"
" type, in either place a file type is configured -- the package's own "
"section, and the object's:"
msgstr ""
"在 ``render:`` 或 ``export:`` 文件类型上写一个 ``filter:`` ，就把同样的意思永久地固定下来，于是一"
"个包可以在整体图形旁边同时签入某个子装配体的图片。它按文件类型声明，可以写在配置文件类型的任一处——包自己的那一节，以及对象的那一节："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:712
msgid ""
"``pc render --filter`` and ``pc export --filter`` override it for one "
"run, the way ``--view`` overrides a configured viewport. A part and a "
"sketch have no links, so a filter over one of them is reported rather "
"than ignored."
msgstr ""
"``pc render --filter`` 和 ``pc export --filter`` 会在单次运行中覆盖它，就像 ``--vi"
"ew`` 覆盖已配置的视口那样。零件和草图没有链接，因此对它们使用过滤器会被报告出来，而不是被忽略。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:717
msgid "Filtering into a new object"
msgstr "过滤成一个新对象"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:719
msgid ""
"``pc filter`` writes a declaration instead: the ASSY file of ``SRC`` with"
" everything the filter drops taken out of it, as ``DST.assy``, declared "
"beside ``SRC``."
msgstr ""
"``pc filter`` 则是写出一份声明：把 ``SRC`` 的 ASSY 文件中被过滤器丢弃的内容全部去掉，写成 ``DST.as"
"sy`` ，并声明在 ``SRC`` 旁边。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:728
msgid ""
"``DST`` is then an object like any other: it renders, it exports, it has "
"a bill of materials, suppliers quote for it, and it is a file somebody "
"can review as a diff. If ``SRC`` is an assembly then ``DST`` is an "
"assembly, and if ``SRC`` is a scene then ``DST`` is a scene -- the kind "
"follows the source. An existing ``DST`` is overwritten; its declaration "
"is left alone when it already points at the same file, so whatever file "
"types were configured for it survive a re-run."
msgstr ""
"此后 ``DST`` 就是一个与其他对象别无二致的对象：它可以渲染、可以导出、有物料清单、供应商可以为它报价，而且它是一个可供人以差异形"
"式审阅的文件。如果 ``SRC`` 是装配体，那么 ``DST`` 也是装配体；如果 ``SRC`` 是场景，那么 ``DST`` 也是"
"场景——类别随源而定。已存在的 ``DST`` 会被覆盖；当它的声明已经指向同一个文件时，该声明保持不变，因此为它配置过的文件类型在重新"
"运行后依然存在。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:735
msgid ""
"The **file** is filtered rather than the built assembly, which is what "
"makes the result an assembly somebody can build: every link kept keeps "
"its ``connect:``, its ``how:``, its parameters and its comments. (That is"
" also why ``pc filter`` needs an Assembly YAML file to work from. A "
"``step`` or ``urdf`` assembly has no links of its own, and ``pc convert "
"assembly -t assy`` is what turns one into a file that does.) The one "
"thing it cannot do is select inside a link that places a part or another "
"package's assembly; it says so and keeps that link whole."
msgstr ""
"被过滤的是 **文件** ，而不是构建出来的装配体，正是这一点使得结果仍然是一个有人能够实际装配出来的装配体：保留下来的每个链接都保留了"
"它的 ``connect:`` 、 ``how:`` 、参数和注释。（这也是 ``pc filter`` 需要有一个 Assembly "
"YAML 文件可供处理的原因。 ``step`` 或 ``urdf`` 类型的装配体没有自己的链接，而 ``pc convert ass"
"embly -t assy`` 正是把这样的装配体转换成带链接的文件的办法。）它唯一做不到的，是在放置了零件、或放置了另一个包的装配体的"
"链接内部进行选择；它会说明这一点，并把该链接整体保留。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:743
msgid ""
"A link whose name was its position has that position **written into** the"
" copy as a ``name:``. Filtering moves links -- the second of five is the "
"first of two once the one above it has gone -- so a position would "
"otherwise rename it, and anything that named it would point at nothing."
msgstr ""
"名称原本就是其位置的链接，该位置会作为 ``name:`` **写入** 副本之中。过滤会使链接发生移动——五个之中的第二个，在它上面那"
"个被去掉之后就成了两个之中的第一个——否则位置就会改变它的名称，而任何指名它的地方都将指向不存在的东西。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:748
msgid ""
"What filtering can break is exactly one thing, and it is checked: **a "
"link that is kept may be connected to a link that was dropped**. ``pc "
"filter`` reports every one of them, naming the line, and so does :ref:`pc"
" lint <assy-lint>` over the file afterwards."
msgstr ""
"过滤可能破坏的恰恰只有一件事，而且这件事是会被检查的： **保留下来的链接可能连接到了被丢弃的链接上** 。 ``pc filter``"
" 会逐一报告这类情况并指出所在行，事后对该文件运行 :ref:`pc lint <assy-lint>` 也会如此。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:757
msgid ""
"Name those links in the filter too, or place the kept ones with "
"``location:``."
msgstr "要么在过滤器中把那些链接也一并指名，要么用 ``location:`` 来放置保留下来的链接。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:763
msgid "Validation"
msgstr "校验"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:765
msgid ""
"ASSY files are checked against a JSON schema "
"(``src/partcad_utils/schema/assy.json``) that describes the document "
"*after* Jinja2 rendering: the node keys above, the shape of an OCCT "
"location, and the fact that ``location``, ``connectPorts`` and "
"``connect`` -- or ``part``, ``assembly`` and ``links`` -- exclude one "
"another."
msgstr ""
"ASSY 文件会依据一份 JSON 模式（ ``src/partcad_utils/schema/assy.json`` ）进行检查，该"
"模式描述的是 Jinja2 渲染 *之后* 的文档：上文列出的那些节点键、OCCT 位置的形式，以及 ``location`` 、 ``"
"connectPorts`` 和 ``connect`` ——或者 ``part`` 、 ``assembly`` 和 ``links`"
"` ——彼此互斥这一事实。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:771
msgid ""
"One thing is checked beside the schema, because no schema can describe "
"it: a ``connect:``/``connectPorts:`` names a link of the **same** "
"``links:`` list, written **above** this node, since that is where PartCAD"
" looks for it as the assembly is built. So does every name in a "
"connection's ``interferes:``, which may be anywhere in the file. A name "
"that is wrong would otherwise be answered, much later, with \"Target part"
" not found\" and a part at the origin."
msgstr ""
"除该模式之外还有一项检查，因为没有任何模式能够描述它： ``connect:`` / ``connectPorts:`` 指名的必须是 "
"**同一个** ``links:`` 列表中、写在本节点 **上方** 的链接，因为在构建装配体时 PartCAD 正是到那里去寻找它的"
"。连接的 ``interferes:`` 中的每一个名称也同样如此，只不过它们可以位于文件中的任何地方。否则，一个写错的名称要等到很久以"
"后，才会以“Target part not found”和一个位于原点的零件作为回应。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:778
msgid ""
"A file read as a **scene** is checked against the same schema with "
"``how`` forbidden. The scene schema is derived from the one above rather "
"than kept beside it, so the two cannot drift apart; only the one rule "
"differs."
msgstr ""
"被当作 **场景** 读取的文件，会依据同一份模式进行检查，只是其中禁用了 ``how`` 。场景模式是由上述模式派生出来的，而不是与它"
"并列单独维护的另一份，因此两者不会逐渐走样；差别只有这一条规则。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:782
#, python-brace-format, python-format
msgid ""
"Because the file on disk is a template rather than the YAML it renders "
"to, the checker masks every Jinja2 construct before parsing: ``{{ expr "
"}}`` becomes a placeholder value and ``{% tag %}`` becomes blanks of the "
"same size. The masked document keeps the exact line and column layout of "
"the file, so a template error, a YAML error and a schema violation are "
"all reported at the character they came from, and a loop or conditional "
"body is checked once. Anything the mask makes unknowable -- what an "
"expression evaluates to, which branch of an ``{% if %}`` is taken -- is "
"left unreported rather than guessed at."
msgstr ""
"由于磁盘上的文件是一个模板、而不是它所渲染出的 YAML，检查器会在解析之前把每一处 Jinja2 结构都遮蔽掉： ``{{ expr "
"}}`` 变成一个占位值， ``{% tag %}`` 变成同样长度的空白。遮蔽后的文档保持与原文件完全一致的行列布局，因此模板错误、Y"
"AML 错误和模式违规都会在它们所出自的那个字符位置上被报告出来，而循环体或条件体只检查一次。凡是遮蔽之后无从得知的东西——表达式求值的"
"结果、 ``{% if %}`` 走的是哪一个分支——都不予报告，而不是去猜测。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:791
msgid "Run the checks over a package from the command line with:"
msgstr "在命令行中对整个包运行这些检查："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:797
msgid "or narrow it to ASSY files only:"
msgstr "或者把范围收窄到只检查 ASSY 文件："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:803
msgid ""
"To check individual files instead, name them. This runs in the ``pc`` "
"process itself -- no daemon, no package to load -- so it answers even "
"when the package does not:"
msgstr ""
"若要改为检查单个文件，把它们的名字写出来即可。这会在 ``pc`` 进程自身中运行——不需要守护进程，也不需要加载包——因此即便包本身给"
"不出答案，它也依然能够作答："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:811
msgid ""
"Add ``--json`` for machine-readable findings (zero-based line and column "
"numbers), and ``--stdin`` to check content that has not been saved, which"
" is how an editor checks the buffer on screen:"
msgstr ""
"加上 ``--json`` 可得到机器可读的检查结果（行号和列号从 0 开始计数），加上 ``--stdin`` 可检查尚未保存的内容—"
"—编辑器正是以这种方式检查屏幕上的缓冲区："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:819
msgid ""
"Whether a single file is checked as an assembly or as a scene is not "
"something the file says, so ``pc lint --file`` works it out from the "
"``partcad.yaml`` files around it: a file at least one scene declares and "
"no assembly declares is a scene. Say so outright with ``--schema``:"
msgstr ""
"单个文件究竟按装配体还是按场景来检查，文件本身并没有说明，因此 ``pc lint --file`` 会从它周围的 ``partcad."
"yaml`` 文件推断出来：如果至少有一个场景声明了某个文件、并且没有任何装配体声明它，那么它就是场景。用 ``--schema`` 可"
"以直接把话说明白："

#: ../../source/assy.rst:828
msgid ""
"The `PartCAD extension for VS Code "
"<https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=PartCAD.partcad-"
"official>`_ runs exactly that while an ASSY file is open and shows the "
"findings in the Problems view. It answers the same question from the "
"package contents it has already loaded, which is the declaration itself "
"rather than a guess at it, and falls back to the command's own answer for"
" a file no loaded package mentions. Set ``partcad.lint.enabled`` to "
"``false`` to turn that off."
msgstr ""
"`面向 VS Code 的 PartCAD 扩展 <https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items"
"?itemName=PartCAD.partcad-official>`_ 在 ASSY 文件打开时运行的正是这项检查，并把检查结果显示"
"在 Problems 视图中。它根据自己已经加载的包内容来回答同一个问题，那就是声明本身、而不是对声明的猜测；对于没有任何已加载的包提及"
"的文件，它会回退到该命令自己给出的答案。把 ``partcad.lint.enabled`` 设为 ``false`` 即可关闭这项功能。"

#: ../../source/assy.rst:835
msgid ""
"``partcad.yaml`` is checked the same way, by the same checker, against "
"the configuration schema (``src/partcad_utils/schema/partcad.json``) -- "
"see :doc:`configuration`. It is a Jinja2 template too, so it is masked "
"before parsing exactly as an ASSY file is, and it has no assembly/scene "
"flavor: nothing points at a package configuration, so ``--schema`` does "
"not apply to one."
msgstr ""
"``partcad.yaml`` 由同一个检查器以同样的方式、依据配置模式（ ``src/partcad_utils/schema/pa"
"rtcad.json`` ）进行检查——参见 :doc:`configuration` 。它同样是一个 Jinja2 模板，因此在解析之"
"前会像 ASSY 文件一样被遮蔽；而且它没有装配体／场景之分：没有任何东西会指向一份包配置，所以 ``--schema`` 对它并不适用。"

